# Shell scripts must keep unix line endings, whatever platform clones them.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks them out with CRLF and the shebang line
# becomes "#!/bin/sh\r". The kernel then looks for an interpreter literally
# named "/bin/sh\r", fails, and reports a file-not-found for a path that
# plainly exists. build-mac.sh strips the carriage returns when it assembles
# the bundle, but a Mac cloning this repo runs the script directly.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Read by macOS, which does not want carriage returns in either.
*.plist text eol=lf
Packaging/README-mac.txt text eol=lf

# Generated icon container. Not text, and must never be line-ending converted.
*.icns binary
